{
  "slug": "notify-sounds",
  "name": "Notify Sounds",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Plays system sounds in Claude Code when a task finishes or when permission is needed, so you don't have to keep watching the terminal. Cross-platform: macOS (afplay), Linux (PulseAudio/PipeWire), Windows (PowerShell SoundPlayer), with terminal-bell fallback. Sub-agent stops are skipped to avoid noise during multi-agent workflows.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **2 hooks**, `Stop`, `Notification`.\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install notify-sounds@claude-community` from `AxGord/claude-notify-sounds`.\n\nA Claude Code plugin that plays system sounds to notify you when Claude Code finishes work or needs permission. Supports macOS, Linux, and Windows.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
